{"diagnosis": "Loopback with divider 64 sends 0xa5 but receives 0xf0, causing TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xf0 want 0xa5 and tohost FAIL 0xdead. Root cause is TX shifter at excerpt line 131 `send_pattern <= {1'b0, send_pattern[9:1]};` shifting 0 instead of idle 1, so the 15-cycle reset dummy and post-byte idle drive ser_tx low creating a false start that mis-frames the receiver for the simpleuart instance (picosoc/picosoc.v:190, picosoc/picosoc.v:201, picosoc/simpleuart.v:20). Changing the fill to 1'b1 restores idle-high and correct framing so 0xa5 is received intact.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -130,5 +130,5 @@
 			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
-				send_pattern <= {1'b0, send_pattern[9:1]};
+				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end
", "expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP, uart loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

